From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:15:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 10153: Fix bounds/overflow bugs in BinaryReader, PEF
 unpacker, InputStreamByteProvider

- BinaryReader.ensureArrayRead: compute count * elementSize in long. The int
  overflow let e.g. readNextIntArray(0x40000001) pass the range check and
  allocate ~4GB from a tiny crafted file (Mach-O DyldChainedStartsOffsets,
  COFF archive linker members, OAT, Swift). Same fix for fixed-length string
  reads (charCount * charLen).
- PEF SectionHeader.getUnpackedData: bounds-check all copies/allocations
  against the unpacked buffer, use readNBytes, reject negative unpacked length
  and overflowing packed values. Previously crafted input produced
  ArrayIndexOutOfBounds/NegativeArraySize exceptions and unbounded allocations.
  Zero-fill past the end is still tolerated (clamped) as before.
- InputStreamByteProvider: use readNBytes/skipNBytes; short reads/skips are
  legal per the InputStream contract and were treated as EOF.

Adds regression tests for all three.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MTr23yTKH3aVpYWc6CPbNF
